**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 
- `ui-smoke`: 
- `ui-tests`: `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataStepTests`

**How to implement.** Correcting the reviewed experiment's setup from the Data step, with its audit note and trail (001 §K 'Corrections: re-point an experiment's setup after the fact (e.g. "LR was at −45"), with a mandatory audit note'; 001 §P `CorrectSetup`; the S9.3 brief). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S9.3. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/DataStepView.fs`: the review panel (step 325) ends with a `Setup:` block: the line `Setup: <the experiment's setup.describe>`; a `DockPanel` whose left child is `Audit note:` and whose fill is a `TextBox` carrying `dataCorrectionNoteField` that shows `model.dataDraft.correctionNote` and sends `SetCorrectionNote` (step 316) on Enter and on losing focus; a `WrapPanel` holding, for each setup of `model.kitSetups` in order whose `reference` is not the experiment's own, the verb `Re-point to <reference.describe>` carrying `dataCorrectSetupChoice setup.name` and sending `CorrectSetup (id, setup.reference, model.dataDraft.correctionNote)`, disabled when `model.kitWrites` is `ControlWithheld`; and, when the experiment's `corrections` are not empty, a vertical `StackPanel` carrying `dataCorrectionTrail` with one wrapping line per correction, oldest first: `<previous.describe> → <corrected.describe>: <note>`. The lab file is never shown as changed, because it is not. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`, in the Data step group, each with a one-line doc: `dataCorrectionNoteField` (`"DataCorrectionNoteField"`) and `dataCorrectionTrail` (`"DataCorrectionTrail"`). `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs`, on `ConstructorUiId` beside `savedSetup` (step 260), with a one-line doc: `static member dataCorrectSetupChoice (name : SetupName) : ConstructorUiId` (`DataCorrectSetup_<name>`). No other control or message is added. Tests, in `DataStepTests`: `the Data step UiIds are the stable intent-named ids` also pins `DataCorrectionNoteField`, `DataCorrectionTrail` and `DataCorrectSetup_Bench B`. New `the correction panel offers every other setup of the kit and lists the audit trail`: over the class's model whose kit holds the setups `Setup 1` (E1's) and `Bench B`, and whose E1 holds one correction `'Setup 0' revision 1 → 'Setup 1' revision 1: LP1 was at 30`, the reviewed E1 shows `Setup: 'Setup 1' revision 1`, one choice `Re-point to 'Bench B' revision 1` and no choice for `Setup 1`, and the trail's one line. `pressing a setup sends CorrectSetup with the typed audit note`: over a recording dispatch with the note field holding `LR was at -45`, pressing the choice of `Bench B` records `CorrectSetup (ExperimentId 1, <Bench B revision 1>, ControlCaption "LR was at -45")`.

**Acceptance.** After the correction panel lands, the reviewed experiment MUST show its setup, every other setup of the kit as a re-point choice sending `CorrectSetup` with the typed audit note, and its audit trail, under the stable ids of `ConstructorUiId`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `the correction panel offers every other setup of the kit and lists the audit trail` and `pressing a setup sends CorrectSetup with the typed audit note`, the count rising by 2, and the changed `the Data step UiIds are the stable intent-named ids`; and build, elevation and the sixteen s31 invariants MUST pass.
